From 00f0bfee3efc84028d5584d4abdf3cdc44b820d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 01:07:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(post): G41/G42 wear cutter compensation on the contour

Compensation gains a third choice, Wear, beside In computer (the
default, unchanged) and In control. Wear walks the same cutter-centre
path Control does (mid-run seam, straight leads at least a radius
long) and records a CompSpan flagged `wear` whose programmed moves are
those centre moves verbatim: the post writes them under G41/G42 Dn /
G40 and the register holds only the wear delta. Control's doors (lead
law, tabs, blends, overlap, keep-down links, open contours/runs, 3+2
tilt) apply under the name "wear compensation".

- motion: Compensation::Wear (+ in_control/label), contour_comp
  push_wear; refusals named per mode.
- cl: CompSpan.wear; project cache DTO keeps it (additive key).
- post: stream `COMP LEFT|RIGHT <um> WEAR`, CompensationType property;
  Fanuc writes the same words plus one per-section comment that D holds
  the wear delta only. Other mill posts and the lathe keep refusing.
- app: generation doors, digest byte 0xC6, project `wear_comp` key.
- ui: the Compensation combo offers Wear (G41/G42) via the op page's
  existing EditOperationParams path.

Pinned by golden nc/contour_wear_comp.nc (Fanuc), app wear_comp
(golden, refusals, undo/redo, project round-trip), motion wear_comp,
post comp round-trip.

Fixes #38

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
